<span id="Description"></span>
== 概要 ==

The [[Image:Sketcher_CreateArcOfParabola.svg|24px]] [[Sketcher_CreateArcOfParabola|Sketcher CreateArcOfParabola]] tool creates a parabolic arc.

[[Image:Sketcher_CreateArcOfParabola_Example.png]]
{{Caption|Parabolic arc (white) with internal geometry (dark yellow)}}

<span id="Usage"></span>
== 使い方 ==

See also: [[Sketcher_Workbench#Drawing_aids|Drawing aids]].

Pos-OVP = Positional [[Sketcher_Preferences#General|On-View-Parameters]].<br>
Dim-OVP = Dimensional On-View-Parameters.

{{Version|26.3}}: OVP support added.

# There are several ways to invoke the tool:
#* Press the {{Button|[[Image:Sketcher_CreateArcOfParabola.svg|16px]] [[Sketcher_CreateArcOfParabola|Parabolic Arc]]}} button.
#* Select the {{MenuCommand|Sketch → Geometries → [[Image:Sketcher_CreateArcOfParabola.svg|16px]] Parabolic Arc}} option from the menu.
#* Use the keyboard shortcut: {{KEY|G}} then {{KEY|J}}.
# The cursor changes to a cross with the tool icon.
# Pick the focus of the arc (labelled 1 in the image above). Or with Pos-OVP: enter its X- and/or Y-coordinate.
# Pick the vertex of the arc (labelled 2 in the image above), this also defines its focal distance. Or with Dim-OVP: enter this distance and/or the angle of the axis of the arc. The angle is relative to the X-axis of the sketch.
# Pick the start point of the arc (labelled 3 or 4 in the image above). Or with Dim-OVP: enter the start parameter of the arc. The parameter is relative to the axis of the arc. No constraint is created for this parameter.
# Pick the endpoint of the arc (labelled 3 or 4 in the image above). Or with Dim-OVP: enter the end parameter of the arc. The parameter is relative to the start of the arc. No constraint is created for this parameter.
# The parabolic arc is created, including a set of internal geometry, and applicable Pos-OVP and Dim-OVP based constraints are added.
# If the tool runs in [[Sketcher_Workbench#Continue_modes|continue mode]]:
## Optionally keep creating arcs.
## To finish, right-click or press {{KEY|Esc}}, or start another geometry or constraint creation tool.

<span id="Notes"></span>
== 補足 ==

* Elements of the internal geometry can be deleted. They can be recreated at any time with [[Sketcher_RestoreInternalAlignmentGeometry|Sketcher RestoreInternalAlignmentGeometry]].


